<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia car registrations rise 5.4 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Australia car registrations rise 5.4 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian new motor vehicle registrations rose a seasonally-adjusted 5.4 percent in February to 58,569, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Economists had expected a rise of about 1.5 percent.  </p>
<p>				   Feb 97     Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted    58,569     55,594     54,769</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		 54,861     46,170     53,232</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates	  56,468     55,700     53,517</p>
<p>NOTE: The bureau said passenger vehicle registrations rose 4.3 percent in February, adjusted, while other vehicles rose 11.4 percent. February registrations rose for the fifth consecutive month in trend terms, with the rate of increase remaining steady over the last three months.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
